  66:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****                  ##### Peripheral Extended control functions #####
  67:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
  68:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** PVD configuration (present on all other devices than STM32F3x8 devices) ***
  69:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     =========================
  70:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..]
  71:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The PVD is used to monitor the VDD power supply by comparing it to a
  72:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           threshold selected by the PVD Level (PLS[2:0] bits in the PWR_CR).
  73:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) A PVDO flag is available to indicate if VDD/VDDA is higher or lower
  74:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           than the PVD threshold. This event is internally connected to the EXTI
  75:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           line16 and can generate an interrupt if enabled. This is done through
  76:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           __HAL_PWR_PVD_EXTI_ENABLE_IT() macro
  77:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The PVD is stopped in Standby mode.
  78:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       -@- PVD is not available on STM32F3x8 Product Line
  79:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  80:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  81:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** Voltage regulator ***
  82:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     =========================
  83:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..]
  84:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The voltage regulator is always enabled after Reset. It works in three different
  85:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           modes.
  86:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           In Run mode, the regulator supplies full power to the 1.8V domain (core, memories
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccPuggnx.s 			page 3


  87:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           and digital peripherals).
  88:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           In Stop mode, the regulator supplies low power to the 1.8V domain, preserving
  89:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           contents of registers and SRAM.
  90:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           In Stop mode, the regulator is powered off. The contents of the registers and SRAM
  91:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           are lost except for the Standby circuitry and the Backup Domain.
  92:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           Note: in the STM32F3x8xx devices, the voltage regulator is bypassed and the
  93:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           microcontroller must be powered from a nominal VDD = 1.8V +/-8U% voltage.
  94:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  95:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  96:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) A PVDO flag is available to indicate if VDD/VDDA is higher or lower
  97:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           than the PVD threshold. This event is internally connected to the EXTI
  98:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           line16 and can generate an interrupt if enabled. This is done through
  99:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           __HAL_PWR_PVD_EXTI_ENABLE_IT() macro
 100:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The PVD is stopped in Standby mode.
 101:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
